1
00:00:05,746 --> 00:00:11,160
Picture a single bowl of liquid, set down
where many kinds of beings can see it.

2
00:00:11,963 --> 00:00:14,940
A human sees clear, refreshing water.

3
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:18,690
A hungry ghost, driven by
deep habits of craving,

4
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:20,946
sees foul pus and blood.

5
00:00:21,026 --> 00:00:24,723
A fish finds the air it breathes
and the home it lives in.

6
00:00:24,803 --> 00:00:27,060
A god tastes delicious nectar.

7
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:31,122
And an awakened being sees
the pure wisdom form of water,

8
00:00:31,202 --> 00:00:33,504
the female Buddha Māmakī.

9
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:38,606
It is one of the oldest examples in
Indian and Tibetan Buddhist thought,

10
00:00:38,686 --> 00:00:42,238
and it asks a simple question.
What is really in the bowl?

11
00:00:43,041 --> 00:00:45,107
Common sense has a ready answer.

12
00:00:45,187 --> 00:00:48,232
Something must be sitting
there first, some raw,

13
00:00:48,312 --> 00:00:52,159
neutral stuff, and each creature
looks at it through its own lens.

14
00:00:52,239 --> 00:00:56,199
Two layers: the hidden thing,
and the many views of it.

15
00:00:57,013 --> 00:01:00,764
The Middle Way of Nāgārjuna,
and the Great Perfection,

16
00:01:00,844 --> 00:01:05,832
Dzogchen, read without a foundation,
both take this picture apart.

17
00:01:05,912 --> 00:01:08,509
Agreement does not need a hidden bedrock.

18
00:01:08,589 --> 00:01:14,012
The thing seen, the one seeing, and the
way they meet are identified together,

19
00:01:14,092 --> 00:01:15,941
each depending on the others.

20
00:01:16,021 --> 00:01:20,656
And the relations between them are just
as impossible to pin down as the things

21
00:01:20,736 --> 00:01:21,936
themselves.

22
00:01:22,745 --> 00:01:26,686
Start with a word we slipped in
without noticing. The liquid.

23
00:01:26,766 --> 00:01:31,632
To say that beings see the same liquid
differently already assumes an object

24
00:01:31,712 --> 00:01:35,953
waiting there, with its own
identity, before anyone meets it.

25
00:01:36,033 --> 00:01:39,173
This is the old idea
that Kant made famous:

26
00:01:39,253 --> 00:01:42,628
a thing in itself,
hidden behind the senses.

27
00:01:43,437 --> 00:01:45,694
So ask what this hidden thing is like.

28
00:01:45,774 --> 00:01:50,028
If it has definite qualities, if it
really is thirst-quenching water,

29
00:01:50,108 --> 00:01:53,493
it cannot explain why the
ghost meets burning pus.

30
00:01:53,573 --> 00:01:58,031
If it has no qualities at all, a
featureless blank cannot cause any

31
00:01:58,111 --> 00:01:59,878
experience whatsoever.

32
00:01:59,958 --> 00:02:02,030
Either way, it does no work.

33
00:02:02,833 --> 00:02:04,274
Someone will push back.

34
00:02:04,354 --> 00:02:08,826
Why not simply wetness, the
quality that water and pus share?

35
00:02:08,906 --> 00:02:12,861
But if wetness is claimed to
exist by itself, it fails.

36
00:02:12,941 --> 00:02:16,421
Wetness in general is an
abstraction made by thought.

37
00:02:16,501 --> 00:02:20,687
In real life it only ever shows
up as this drinkable water,

38
00:02:20,767 --> 00:02:24,261
this foul pus, this water a fish lives in.

39
00:02:24,341 --> 00:02:27,454
And if wetness is only an
agreed reference point,

40
00:02:27,534 --> 00:02:29,845
it is no longer a hidden thing at all.

41
00:02:29,925 --> 00:02:32,580
It is a useful label for comparing views.

42
00:02:33,402 --> 00:02:37,195
What Nāgārjuna's analysis
targets is called svabhāva,

43
00:02:37,275 --> 00:02:42,439
own nature: a nature a thing would have
all by itself, depending on nothing.

44
00:02:42,519 --> 00:02:47,480
A neutral substance beneath appearances
is just that imagined nature in a modest

45
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,760
disguise.

46
00:02:49,510 --> 00:02:51,496
Then a real question remains.

47
00:02:51,576 --> 00:02:56,061
If there is no hidden object, why do
humans agree so reliably that the liquid

48
00:02:56,141 --> 00:03:01,568
is water? Why doesn't the shared world
fall apart into private fantasies?

49
00:03:02,389 --> 00:03:06,439
The Indian master Candrakīrti
turns the question around.

50
00:03:06,519 --> 00:03:09,048
Agreement does not prove a hidden object.

51
00:03:09,128 --> 00:03:13,998
Shared, reliable agreement is
simply what everyday truth is.

52
00:03:14,814 --> 00:03:17,302
He also refuses the opposite move.

53
00:03:17,382 --> 00:03:22,017
The Mind-Only view tried to solve the
puzzle by removing outer objects and

54
00:03:22,097 --> 00:03:25,386
making a truly real
consciousness the foundation.

55
00:03:25,466 --> 00:03:29,123
But a seeing cannot be
identified without what is seen,

56
00:03:29,203 --> 00:03:33,688
and an object cannot be identified
without the senses that pick it out.

57
00:03:33,768 --> 00:03:36,446
Neither mind nor matter comes first.

58
00:03:36,526 --> 00:03:41,378
Making the mind the container of
everything is as mistaken as making matter

59
00:03:41,458 --> 00:03:42,658
the container.

60
00:03:43,426 --> 00:03:46,594
Within everyday truth,
mistakes are still caught.

61
00:03:46,674 --> 00:03:50,153
A person with jaundice sees a
white conch shell as yellow,

62
00:03:50,233 --> 00:03:53,536
and other people, with
healthy eyes, correct them.

63
00:03:53,616 --> 00:03:55,751
But notice where that judgement is made.

64
00:03:55,831 --> 00:03:58,183
It is made within one kind of being.

65
00:03:58,263 --> 00:04:01,186
The hungry ghost is not a jaundiced human.

66
00:04:01,266 --> 00:04:05,303
By the standards of its own
kind, its senses work normally.

67
00:04:05,383 --> 00:04:07,966
It is not suffering an illusion of water.

68
00:04:08,046 --> 00:04:11,829
For the ghost, the liquid
really does function as pus.

69
00:04:12,649 --> 00:04:14,267
So what of the bowl itself?

70
00:04:14,347 --> 00:04:18,805
In this article's own terms, what is
denied is a shared base that exists by

71
00:04:18,885 --> 00:04:22,093
itself, there before anyone perceives it.

72
00:04:22,173 --> 00:04:24,715
What is kept is a working reference point:

73
00:04:24,795 --> 00:04:29,417
a label, made from within one frame,
for the place where different ways of

74
00:04:29,497 --> 00:04:31,984
appearing meet and can be compared.

75
00:04:32,064 --> 00:04:35,508
Its job is to coordinate,
not to sit underneath.

76
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:39,280
The bowl example did not
begin in the Middle Way.

77
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:45,360
Vasubandhu, in his Twenty Verses, used
the hungry ghosts to defend Mind-Only.

78
00:04:45,692 --> 00:04:50,598
Ghosts with the same karma all see
a river of pus together, he said.

79
00:04:50,678 --> 00:04:55,693
Shared karma, ripening in consciousness,
explains shared experience,

80
00:04:55,773 --> 00:04:58,632
and no river outside the mind is needed.

81
00:04:59,446 --> 00:05:03,062
That answers the question by
making consciousness the floor.

82
00:05:03,142 --> 00:05:06,133
Candrakīrti turned the example around.

83
00:05:06,213 --> 00:05:09,380
Just as the object does
not exist on its own,

84
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:12,220
he concluded, neither does the mind.

85
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:16,662
The river of pus and the seeing
of it stand or fall together.

86
00:05:16,742 --> 00:05:20,508
So the bowl does not show that
the world is inside the mind.

87
00:05:20,588 --> 00:05:24,425
It shows that neither the world
nor the mind is the floor.

88
00:05:25,237 --> 00:05:28,064
Agreement also needs others to agree with.

89
00:05:28,144 --> 00:05:32,100
Indian logicians debated whether
other minds could be proven,

90
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:35,659
and both sides assumed that
my own experience is certain,

91
00:05:35,739 --> 00:05:37,358
and yours only inferred.

92
00:05:37,438 --> 00:05:39,966
The Middle Way refuses that imbalance.

93
00:05:40,046 --> 00:05:44,545
Looked for closely, my stream of
mind is no more findable than yours,

94
00:05:44,625 --> 00:05:46,706
and both work in daily life.

95
00:05:46,786 --> 00:05:50,188
Other observers are identified
together with this one,

96
00:05:50,277 --> 00:05:53,137
as long is identified together with short.

97
00:05:53,945 --> 00:05:55,713
A critic can press further.

98
00:05:55,793 --> 00:05:59,598
Senses count as healthy when they
agree with others of their kind,

99
00:05:59,678 --> 00:06:04,204
and the kind is defined by sharing
those senses. Isn't that circular?

100
00:06:04,284 --> 00:06:06,895
It is, and the circle is not a flaw.

101
00:06:06,975 --> 00:06:12,126
It would be fatal only if agreement had to
rest on a final judge outside every point

102
00:06:12,206 --> 00:06:14,694
of view. There is no such judge.

103
00:06:14,774 --> 00:06:19,082
Nothing is being built on a foundation,
so no foundation is missing.

104
00:06:19,162 --> 00:06:22,751
Wittgenstein reached a
similar point: we agree,

105
00:06:22,831 --> 00:06:25,645
not in opinions, but in form of life.

106
00:06:25,725 --> 00:06:28,964
And inside the circle,
correction is still real.

107
00:06:29,821 --> 00:06:33,709
For humans, much of this
agreement is carried by language.

108
00:06:33,789 --> 00:06:36,752
A child learns the word
water because it works.

109
00:06:36,832 --> 00:06:39,049
Say it, and a glass arrives.

110
00:06:39,129 --> 00:06:43,953
Yet language is also where the habit
of making things solid is strongest.

111
00:06:44,033 --> 00:06:49,963
The noun, the bowl, seems to point at
one solid thing behind every view of it.

112
00:06:50,771 --> 00:06:54,962
Dzogchen describes the same freedom
from the side of experience.

113
00:06:55,781 --> 00:06:58,921
In the Dzogchen of Longchenpa and Mipham,

114
00:06:59,001 --> 00:07:01,638
the basis is primordially pure.

115
00:07:01,718 --> 00:07:05,266
It is not a hidden block
of stuff, a cosmic mind,

116
00:07:05,346 --> 00:07:07,195
or a starting point of the world.

117
00:07:07,275 --> 00:07:11,652
Longchenpa says it is called a ground
only from a relative point of view.

118
00:07:11,732 --> 00:07:15,882
In the way things are, it is
empty of being any ground at all.

119
00:07:16,689 --> 00:07:18,647
Appearances are called display.

120
00:07:18,727 --> 00:07:22,424
And display is not the display
of something standing behind it.

121
00:07:22,504 --> 00:07:28,504
It is dependent arising itself, vivid
and unobstructed, with nothing behind it.

122
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:31,554
Even the feeling of
being a subject inside,

123
00:07:31,634 --> 00:07:34,774
looking out at a world,
is part of the display,

124
00:07:34,854 --> 00:07:37,782
arising together with the object outside.

125
00:07:38,581 --> 00:07:43,270
Knowing awareness, rigpa, is not
a projector throwing out a world.

126
00:07:43,350 --> 00:07:45,838
It is not a subtle stuff behind appearing.

127
00:07:45,918 --> 00:07:50,281
It is the knowing of the basis:
knowing appearing as unfixed,

128
00:07:50,361 --> 00:07:52,033
dependent and empty.

129
00:07:52,113 --> 00:07:55,009
The clarity belongs to
the appearing itself,

130
00:07:55,089 --> 00:07:57,581
and like the appearing, it is empty.

131
00:07:58,398 --> 00:08:02,055
The traditions divide on
whether awareness knows itself.

132
00:08:02,135 --> 00:08:05,384
Candrakīrti rejected
self-knowing awareness,

133
00:08:05,464 --> 00:08:10,818
and Śāntideva made the argument famous
with a sword that cannot cut itself.

134
00:08:10,898 --> 00:08:14,595
In the author's own reading,
this article follows Mipham.

135
00:08:14,675 --> 00:08:17,557
Ultimately, self-knowing cannot be found,

136
00:08:17,637 --> 00:08:19,297
like everything else.

137
00:08:19,377 --> 00:08:22,884
Conventionally, it stays
a useful everyday term,

138
00:08:22,964 --> 00:08:26,674
to explain memory and the
immediacy of experience,

139
00:08:26,754 --> 00:08:30,293
without an endless chain
of minds watching minds.

140
00:08:31,101 --> 00:08:35,246
Mipham also separates ordinary
vision from pure vision.

141
00:08:35,326 --> 00:08:40,436
Within ordinary vision, the vision
of beings in the cycle of existence,

142
00:08:40,516 --> 00:08:44,010
no kind of being has the
last word over another.

143
00:08:44,090 --> 00:08:46,374
Even the gods' nectar belongs here.

144
00:08:46,454 --> 00:08:51,555
Pure vision is clearer: there,
the liquid appears as Māmakī.

145
00:08:51,644 --> 00:08:54,974
But pure vision is not
a window onto a bedrock.

146
00:08:55,054 --> 00:08:59,648
It is itself empty, and Māmakī
has no nature of her own.

147
00:08:59,728 --> 00:09:03,928
It is clearer because it sees without
the distortion that splits the world into

148
00:09:04,008 --> 00:09:06,650
solid subjects and solid things.

149
00:09:07,465 --> 00:09:10,102
Modern physics offers echoes of this.

150
00:09:10,182 --> 00:09:12,430
Only echoes, not proofs.

151
00:09:13,256 --> 00:09:17,632
For Karen Barad, things do not
exist first and then interact.

152
00:09:17,712 --> 00:09:20,499
They emerge through what
she calls intra-action.

153
00:09:20,579 --> 00:09:23,624
So there is no liquid sitting
there before the measurement.

154
00:09:23,704 --> 00:09:26,831
The human drinker and the
water appear together,

155
00:09:26,911 --> 00:09:30,409
and the suffering ghost and
the pus appear together.

156
00:09:31,209 --> 00:09:34,267
In Carlo Rovelli's
relational quantum mechanics,

157
00:09:34,347 --> 00:09:38,642
physical quantities have values
only relative to another system.

158
00:09:38,722 --> 00:09:41,591
How, then, do two observers agree?

159
00:09:41,671 --> 00:09:46,224
With Emily Adlam, Rovelli answered
with cross-perspective links.

160
00:09:46,304 --> 00:09:50,381
If one observer records a value and
a second later checks the record,

161
00:09:50,461 --> 00:09:55,164
the two will match. Agreement comes
from checking across perspectives,

162
00:09:55,244 --> 00:09:57,990
much as healthy senses
confirm one another,

163
00:09:58,070 --> 00:10:00,264
not from a hidden state underneath.

164
00:10:01,082 --> 00:10:04,983
But neither theory should be read as
saying that relations are what is really

165
00:10:05,063 --> 00:10:07,959
there. That would only
build another floor.

166
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:13,040
Nāgārjuna examined contact itself
and found it cannot be found either.

167
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:16,994
Relations and the things
related are identified together,

168
00:10:17,074 --> 00:10:18,846
and neither is the ground.

169
00:10:19,649 --> 00:10:22,476
If appearances depend
on channels of contact,

170
00:10:22,556 --> 00:10:26,349
what happens when a being shares
almost no channel with something?

171
00:10:26,429 --> 00:10:28,282
Contact comes in degrees.

172
00:10:29,085 --> 00:10:33,828
A tick responds mainly to three
signals: the smell of mammal sweat,

173
00:10:33,908 --> 00:10:36,369
the warmth of a body, and hair.

174
00:10:36,449 --> 00:10:39,589
A pool of clear spring
water has none of these,

175
00:10:39,669 --> 00:10:42,048
so it never appears in the tick's world.

176
00:10:42,128 --> 00:10:44,331
Yet the tick can still drown in it.

177
00:10:44,411 --> 00:10:48,407
Dark matter passes through the Earth
as if the planet were not there,

178
00:10:48,487 --> 00:10:51,314
yet gravity still bends its path.

179
00:10:51,394 --> 00:10:55,689
A neutrino can pass through lead
on the order of a light year thick.

180
00:10:55,769 --> 00:10:58,217
The lead is neither a wall nor nothing.

181
00:10:58,297 --> 00:11:00,952
It is a region of very weak contact.

182
00:11:01,766 --> 00:11:06,061
The bowl is not erased just because
some being fails to register it.

183
00:11:06,141 --> 00:11:10,246
Everyday existence does not wait
for someone to be naming it.

184
00:11:10,326 --> 00:11:13,167
But what appears there, nourishment, pus,

185
00:11:13,247 --> 00:11:18,294
a barrier or an open passage, depends on
which channels are active in the meeting.

186
00:11:19,109 --> 00:11:22,099
The hardest test is
contact between worlds.

187
00:11:22,179 --> 00:11:27,480
In offerings to hungry ghosts, water
is blessed with a mantra and given,

188
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:30,958
and the tradition holds that
it reaches them as nectar.

189
00:11:31,038 --> 00:11:33,186
Not by a substance that travels.

190
00:11:33,266 --> 00:11:36,841
Nothing passes from the human
bowl into the ghost's mouth,

191
00:11:36,921 --> 00:11:41,420
just as nothing passes from the
evening flame into the midnight flame.

192
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:43,852
The giving belongs to the human world.

193
00:11:43,932 --> 00:11:46,203
The relief belongs to the ghost's.

194
00:11:46,283 --> 00:11:51,357
They are linked as condition and result,
with no common object underneath.

195
00:11:52,161 --> 00:11:53,983
Two cautions belong here.

196
00:11:54,063 --> 00:11:56,904
This does not prove that
such practices work.

197
00:11:56,984 --> 00:12:00,994
It only asks what the claim would
mean without a hidden substance.

198
00:12:01,074 --> 00:12:04,730
And the mantra is not a
power living inside sounds,

199
00:12:04,810 --> 00:12:07,923
any more than the power
to open lives in a key,

200
00:12:08,003 --> 00:12:11,134
apart from the lock,
the hand and the door.

201
00:12:11,954 --> 00:12:15,013
Why do we cling so hard
to an object underneath?

202
00:12:15,093 --> 00:12:16,861
Because of the container myth.

203
00:12:16,941 --> 00:12:21,779
We picture space as an empty box,
place a solid object in the middle,

204
00:12:21,859 --> 00:12:26,752
and put observers around it who must
either see the real thing or be fooled.

205
00:12:26,832 --> 00:12:31,005
In Einstein's theory, spacetime
is not an empty stage.

206
00:12:31,085 --> 00:12:33,518
It is the gravitational field itself.

207
00:12:33,598 --> 00:12:38,695
And Nāgārjuna shows that space cannot
exist before its own defining mark,

208
00:12:38,775 --> 00:12:40,747
the absence of obstruction.

209
00:12:40,827 --> 00:12:45,819
When the box goes, the puzzle of one
object seen many ways goes with it.

210
00:12:46,638 --> 00:12:52,333
One last question. If there is no ultimate
ground, why is the world so orderly?

211
00:12:52,413 --> 00:12:55,231
Barley seeds grow barley, not rice.

212
00:12:55,361 --> 00:12:57,672
Fire burns and does not freeze.

213
00:12:57,752 --> 00:13:01,997
Being empty of a fixed nature
does not make anything arbitrary.

214
00:13:02,818 --> 00:13:06,448
But emptiness is not what makes
cause and effect work either.

215
00:13:06,528 --> 00:13:09,808
Emptiness enables nothing
and explains nothing.

216
00:13:09,911 --> 00:13:13,064
Things never needed a fixed
essence in order to work.

217
00:13:13,144 --> 00:13:16,135
Something with a fixed
essence could never arise,

218
00:13:16,215 --> 00:13:18,001
change or end.

219
00:13:18,830 --> 00:13:22,609
Press further, and ask why
there is a web of causes at all,

220
00:13:22,689 --> 00:13:27,460
and the question treats the whole web as
one thing that needs an outside cause.

221
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:32,718
But the whole is a label too, and
dependent arising has no first beginning.

222
00:13:32,798 --> 00:13:37,179
The question does not uncover a
hidden answer. It runs out of steam.

223
00:13:37,997 --> 00:13:39,642
So this is not nihilism.

224
00:13:39,722 --> 00:13:44,928
It is not idealism, because the mind
is as empty as the things it meets.

225
00:13:45,008 --> 00:13:49,452
And it is not anything goes, because
everyday truth works with reliable

226
00:13:49,532 --> 00:13:54,860
regularity. What is removed is only
the anxious demand for a foundation,

227
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:59,022
a dead, unmoving ballast
beneath the living display.

228
00:13:59,841 --> 00:14:02,383
It also matters beyond philosophy.

229
00:14:02,463 --> 00:14:05,617
If the ghost's pus is
really pus for the ghost,

230
00:14:05,697 --> 00:14:08,850
its suffering is not a
mistake to be explained away.

231
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:14,462
No point of view owns the real world, so
no being's world can be dismissed as only

232
00:14:14,542 --> 00:14:19,027
theirs. That is why compassion makes
sense without a self behind it.

233
00:14:19,107 --> 00:14:22,464
Emptiness takes nothing
away from others' suffering,

234
00:14:22,545 --> 00:14:24,480
or from the wish to relieve it.

235
00:14:25,285 --> 00:14:30,653
Nāgārjuna put it in one line, where
the key word means fits, or works.

236
00:14:30,733 --> 00:14:33,918
For whom emptiness
works, everything works.

237
00:14:34,721 --> 00:14:39,464
And from the side of Dzogchen: when
appearances are recognised as display,

238
00:14:39,544 --> 00:14:42,942
with no solid subject
grasping a solid object,

239
00:14:43,022 --> 00:14:46,094
appearing is met as it always was.

240
00:14:46,175 --> 00:14:49,591
Vivid, unproduced, and not found anywhere.

241
00:14:50,397 --> 00:14:54,882
Everyday life does not carry on
in spite of having no foundation.

242
00:14:54,962 --> 00:14:58,949
And it does not appear because
it has none. It never needed one.

